 DESQview 2.8 - READ.ME File

 Congratulations on installing the latest version of DESQview, the
 powerful multitasking multi-windowing software from Quarterdeck!
 PLEASE TAKE A MOMENT TO REVIEW THIS FILE which contains some
 last-minute information, compatibility notes, and important
 corrections to the manual. You may want to print this file for
 future reference.  To do this, switch to the directory into which
 you installed DESQview (probably \DV) and type "COPY READ.ME PRN:"
 at the DOS prompt.

 If you are installing DESQview 386, ensure that you begin the
 installation process with the DESQview diskette, rather than the
 QEMM diskette.  You will be asked to install QEMM at the end of
 the DESQview installation process; although we recommend updating
 your copy of QEMM, you need not follow this step if QEMM is
 already present on your system.  Since the DESQview and QEMM
 components of DESQview 386 are effectively separate products,
 you will be asked to provide registration information for each.

 You should also take a moment to review to the QEMM README file.
 Look for the file README.TXT in the directory into which you
 installed QEMM (probably \QEMM).

